# Legacy data that deliberately left git history (commit 8a348e6): the six
# superseded 4-action/2-action inverse experiments, early pilots, and the
# planning_comm side project. Kept local-only; see data/legacy/README.md.
# The forward-planning and Study 1a pilot CSVs under data/legacy/ remain
# tracked.
data/legacy/*_alt/
data/legacy/*_noalt/
data/legacy/pilots/
data/legacy/planning_comm/

# Non-fitted model-behavior visualizations (parameter sweeps + belief-update
# plots at hand-picked params). Exploratory and not part of the fit pipeline;
# regenerate from the scripts in model/model_viz_nonfit/. Kept local.
model/model_viz_nonfit/

# Live-run CV fold checkpoint (lets an interrupted LOSO run resume; deleted
# when the run's final outputs are written). Transient by design — the
# committed CV artifacts are the cv_* outputs, never this side file. Both the
# study root and the alt/<tag>/ configs write one.
model/outputs/*/cv_checkpoint.jsonl
model/outputs/*/alt/*/cv_checkpoint.jsonl

# Cross-study parameter-transfer runs (model/cv/transfer.py). Sixteen
# (pair x arm) CV output sets at ~2.8 MB each, for an exploratory analysis that
# is in no preregistration — the same reasoning that keeps the other
# exploratory alt/ configs out of the repo, and unlike the preregistered-model
# (uniform-noreweight) outputs, which are committed because the paper quotes
# numbers derived from them. Regenerate with `make transfer`; the summary the
# result is read from, model/outputs/transfer/transfer_summary.json, is small
# and IS committed. If the analysis becomes paper material, promote it the same
# way the eta = 0 run was.
model/outputs/*/alt/transfer-*/

# Pooled cross-experiment CV runs (model/cv/pooled.py), same reasoning as the
# transfer runs above: exploratory, in no preregistration, and ~1.7 MB per
# group. Regenerate with `make pooled`; the summary the result is read from,
# model/outputs/pooled/, is small and IS committed.
model/outputs/*/alt/pooled-*/

# Diagnostic-arm LM elicitations, written by `generate_alternatives.py
# --arm-output-only` and `score_merged.py --arm`. These exist to evaluate a
# prompt edit side-by-side against the committed tables without displacing
# them, so they are throwaway by construction: a K=1 smoke, a candidate
# vintage, an arm that may never be adopted. The tables the reported fits read
# are the unsuffixed lm_alternatives/lm_runs files, which stay committed. If an
# arm IS adopted, it is promoted by re-eliciting into the canonical filenames,
# never by committing the diag vintage.
# One glob rather than per-suffix rules: the sidecars have grown (.rationale,
# .empty_units, .manifest) and a saved-aside vintage adds an infix, both of which
# escaped the narrower patterns. No canonical filename contains "_diag".
model/outputs/lm/*/*_diag*

